  "longBusinessSummary": "Aumann AG manufactures and sells specialized machines and production lines for electromobility, automation, and robot applications in Germany, rest of Europe, the United States, Canada, Mexico, China, and internationally. It operates through two segments: E-Mobility and Next Automation. The E-Mobility segment provides energy storage and conversion systems, electric traction drive, associated power electronics, power-on-demand aggregates, auxiliary motors, as well as electronic components in the field of sensor technology and control. This segment also offers laminating and coating systems for electrodes, and membrane-electrode assembly production. The Next Automation segment develops and produces automated manufacturing solutions for various industries, such as clean tech, aerospace, and life sciences. This segment also provides automated production lines for household appliances, industrial electric motors, photovoltaic modules, hydrogen electrolysers and wind turbines; and systems to produce drive components that reduce the CO2 emissions of vehicles with combustion engines. Aumann AG was founded in 1936 and is headquartered in Beelen, Germany.",
